  "id": "retinal-pigment-epithelium",
  "term": "retinal pigment epithelium",
  "definition": "The retinal pigment epithelium is a single layer of pigment-containing cells in the retina that lies next to the outer parts of photoreceptor cells. It supports these light-sensing cells by helping move nutrients, clearing shed cell material, and helping keep the retina attached.",
